WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:11.610
<i>Pull the rope with all your might</i>

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:20.990
<i>And bring that boat ashore</i>

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.220
<i>So that my beloved...</i>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.980
<i>I will never be able to hear</i>

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.570
<i>their cheers and applause again.</i>

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:13.980
Songstress of Sleep

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.720
The extermination of the Incarnates 
is proceeding smoothly.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.140
We estimate that within six months—

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.470
That's too long.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.940
Tell them to take care of 
it within three months.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.450
Y-Yes, sir.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:33.280
He's rather ruthless, considering it's his 
son who's leading the extermination unit.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.210
Now that the Incarnate project has failed,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.140
we need a new banner to 
unite the country under.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.660
And he's given that task to his own son?

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.760
His son will save the nation.
 He's using his son as a political pawn.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.890
President Richard Withers... 
What a terrifying man.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.610
Captain Claude.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.190
When will the supply ships arrive?

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.940
I believe it'll take four to five days.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.430
That's too long!

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.820
There is little we can do.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.140
Our equipment is rather special, 
so there are only a few supply routes.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.590
Sorry you have to help me 
with these errands.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.630
Oh, it's fine. I'm used 
to doing stuff like this.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.010
I'm stronger than I look, you know.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.510
Right now, you look like a 
common girl from any town.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.550
Huh?

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.840
You're making fun of me, aren't you, Liza?!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.250
I'd say it's a compliment.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.180
It's probably better to look like that 
than like a bloodthirsty murderer.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.560
I mean, you've got the goods.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.700
If you keep working hard, you can be 
as beautiful as me someday... maybe.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.360
Liza...

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.860
You're going to have to work hard, though.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.040
Well, I'm gonna head back to our camp!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.480
It's so beautiful...

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.300
Hank...

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:12.540
<i>Pull the rope with all your might</i>

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:22.520
<i>And bring that boat ashore</i>

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:35.030
<i>So that my beloved can come home</i>

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.370
<i>An Incarnate?!</i>

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:44.570
<i>Without losing their way</i>

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.170
Don't move.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.570
Leave this place now.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.920
Forget everything you saw here.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.100
Otherwise...

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:47.630
Don't.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.050
Don't, Charles.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.840
Put the gun down.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.150
Trice! Why are you singing?

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.020
Do you want the people in town to find you?

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.320
Um... I'm John William Bancroft's daughter.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.190
I see... So Will is...

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.160
Yes. I was with him in his final moments.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.620
I see.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.620
Sorry for scaring you earlier, miss.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:22.260
The government is dead set on 
hunting down all Incarnates.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.890
We have to do everything we can

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.560
to make sure the townsfolk and 
the government don't find her.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:27.840
The townsfolk, too?

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.150
The government's put a bounty on her.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.460
If people tell them where she is, 
they'll get a cash reward.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.780
No...

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:38.300
But more than that, everyone's scared.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.930
The wounds from the war 
still haven't healed.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:47.340
Everyone's nervous that another war
 could break out at any second.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.350
That's why no one can find out about her.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.690
Um, are you two...

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.090
I run a bar in town, 
and Trice was the singer there.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.060
A singer?!

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.760
I-I've never met one before!

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.740
No wonder your voice is so lovely!

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.440
That's all in the past.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:13.160
Back then, singing was my everything.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:19.530
I would sing my songs upon a dazzling 
stage in front of a huge crowd.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:24.760
No matter how sad someone looked, 
they would smile when they heard me sing.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.670
That was my pride. That was where I belonged.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.960
But then...

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.850
The war happened, and everything changed.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.430
All of the townspeople were living 
in fear of an unknown future,

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.960
and were desperate just 
to live through each day.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.580
My songs became unnecessary.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:51.440
Then, one day, I was told that 
I had a special power.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.730
A tremendous power that could 
even help end the war.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.490
So I went to the battlefield,

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.620
because I didn't want to 
live in an age without song.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.920
Thank you, Danny.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.810
I killed many on the battlefield.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:32.650
When we returned, our country 
regarded us as heroes...

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:41.650
But we were no longer human to them.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:51.590
No one wanted to hear a monster sing.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.420
I've lived here ever since.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.950
But that's coming to an end, too.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.190
Trice!

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.490
I can't just keep hiding.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.070
They'll find me someday.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:10.660
Besides...

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:15.300
What's the point of living if I can't sing?

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:22.200
Cheer up! You can't lose hope!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:26.020
Um... I'm going to be in this town for a while.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.000
May I come visit you again?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.520
Visit me again?

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.890
My name is Schaal. What's yours?

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.690
Beatrice. Everyone calls me Trice.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.650
I'll come visit again, Trice,
so let's talk more next time!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.000
There has to be something 
I can do for Trice.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:52.960
Yeah!

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.030
Good morning, Trice!

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.150
Welcome, Schaal.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.670
Come over here.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.040
Be careful!

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.840
Excellent.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.880
With this fortress and the Incarnates, 
there's no way the North can outdo us.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:48.820
Master Cain, when are they going to come?

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.330
Very soon.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:55.190
Really? Hank doesn't like onions?

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.000
No.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.180
I had no idea!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.980
There's something he hates even more.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.160
What?

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.100
Well...

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.290
What?!

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:10.260
Your expressions change so readily.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.830
You know... There was something I wished to do.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:21.130
I wanted to sing in front of people again,

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.010
just like I used to.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.270
But no one will listen to me now, 
because they're afraid of how I look.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:34.310
Your appearance doesn't matter! 
You have such a lovely voice.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:40.660
I'm sure everyone would love 
to hear you sing again someday.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.470
Thank you.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.110
Where were you?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.420
Er, I was...

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.850
You shouldn't wander around outside too much.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.630
Why is that?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:06.120
The people here are 
extremely wary of soldiers.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.430
They're afraid another 
war might break out.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:13.390
Anxiety will lead people 
to do unexpected things.

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:17.010
We'd gladly leave if we could...

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.370
We need to exterminate all of the 
Incarnates as soon as possible.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.970
Is that all for the sake of your mission?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.190
What do you mean by that?

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:29.710
Er... How do I put this?

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.040
I have an older brother.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.670
His name is Cain.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:42.130
The one who leads New Patria along with 
the Incarnates is my older brother.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.210
What?!

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:46.870
He betrayed me and the rest 
of the Withers family.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.480
As his younger brother, I will take him down.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.110
That is my duty.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.270
You should understand how I feel.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:54.800
Huh?

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.020
You did well, shooting your father.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.630
I'll do what I must, as well.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.190
I will exterminate all of the Incarnates...

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.610
including my brother and Hank Henriette.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.470
Sorry, we're not open until tonight.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.650
Charles, are you hiding something from us?

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:46.680
Someone saw you on the beach, 
and they said they heard a strange song.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:54.200
I heard that the guys staying near the beach 
are the Incarnate extermination squad.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.740
We're going to take a look around your bar.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:31.660
Charles.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:36.870
Charles, I'm thinking 
about leaving this town.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:42.800
Once enough time passes and people 
are ready to accept us again...

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.290
I'll come back here.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.270
And then...

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.320
I'll sing up on that stage again!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:57.970
Charles!

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.220
How did this happen?!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.320
Run, Trice...

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.860
The men from town will be here soon...

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:11.660
Please don't hold this against them.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:18.610
They're just so exhausted that the 
thought of facing the future is painful.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.970
Trice...

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.160
Trice...

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:32.090
I don't think I'll be able to play 
the piano for you anymore...

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:36.110
I'm... sorry...

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.070
There's a fire near the port!

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:51.030
<i>Pull the rope with all your might</i>

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.100
Huh? What's that?

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:44.840
A song?

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.050
This is...

00:14:52.120 --> 00:15:00.930
<i>And bring that boat ashore</i>

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:04.050
Ah, so it <i>is</i> her...

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:06.380
<i>So that my beloved...</i>

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.210
She must've come back from the war...

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.890
This is...

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:17.570
They're still breathing. 
They appear to just be in a deep sleep.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.150
They're asleep?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.330
The Incarnate Siren!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:26.370
I'm pretty sure she had the ability 
to make people fall asleep.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:27.810
Split up and find her!

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:28.530
Yes, sir!

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:33.850
<i>...can come home</i>

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:43.750
<i>Without losing their way</i>

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.300
Why, you—

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:54.920
<i>Let the foghorn sound</i>

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.770
Trice!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.080
<i>And—</i>

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.560
Why?! Why are you doing this?!

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.190
Look, Schaal!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.870
Everyone looks so peaceful 
and happy as they sleep.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:16.590
They don't have to be scared of the 
painful future anymore... ever again.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.790
My song saved them all!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:24.010
There are no cheers or applause, 
but this stage is just for me!

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.260
Isn't it wonderful?

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.960
No... No!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.750
This isn't the Trice I wanted to see!

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.610
Trice!

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:46.640
Wait! Don't go alone!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.700
Trice.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.880
Isn't this stage a mess?

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.730
I used to sing here.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:11.160
Before standing on this stage, 
I had absolutely nothing.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:14.710
I just tried to avert my eyes 
from the pain every day.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:20.590
But this stage gave me... my reason to live.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:25.020
But I can't stand on it 
anymore with this body.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:28.850
No one will listen to my song.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:35.610
You're not going to listen 
to me sing either, are you?

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.980
When he returned from the war, 
my father had lost his ability to speak.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:48.550
But still, I could still feel his kindness.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:56.100
So I believe you can sing, too! 
Just like you used to!

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.880
Please, let me hear you sing.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.730
Schaal, I—

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.880
She's still breathing! Finish her off!

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:20.640
Trice!

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.360
Wait!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:30.070
No! This song is different!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.500
Trice...

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:50.400
<i>My beloved is on a ship</i>

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:59.660
<i>That shall never return</i>

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:11.380
<i>I'll continue to shine this light</i>

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:22.370
<i>And finally greet my beloved</i>

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:32.630
<i>So that we can sing together again</i>

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:42.960
<i>On that beach once more</i>

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.430
Trice...

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:57.080
Schaal, how was that?

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:00.280
It was lovely.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:16.680
Be careful! Handle that carefully!

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.350
I see. Thank you.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:27.820
Hank Henriette's tracks have been 
found in the central mountains.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:29.490
Really?!

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.400
Let me make one thing clear.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:34.910
The next time you get in the way,
 we'll shoot through you.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.950
I thought you were going to shoot her.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.260
That's what you should've done.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:46.600
I wanted to save her.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.150
We were only together for a short time,

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:54.320
but still, she was a dear friend to me.

00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:15.090
Please, forgive me...
 I was starving... I couldn't help it.

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:17.140
I can't.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:20.360
Those who have lost 
their souls shall be slain.

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.520
Vic, fulfill our oath!

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:44.390
I don't want to die!

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:48.510
I'm just... I'm just so hungry...

00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:12.570
I will... fulfill our oath...

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:24.370
I found you...

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:26.550
Captain...

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:27.560
Captain Hank...

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:29.970
Hank, I will fulfill...

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:30.950
This sucks...

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:33.170
I don't want to give up.

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:38.730
I am the Incarnate Garm!

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
The Hound of Hell's Gate
